  "details": "This page explains the Event Execution order in VRChat:\n\nhttps://creators.vrchat.com/worlds/udon/event-execution-order/\n\nIn normal Unity C#, each step is done for all active GameObjects. However, in VRChat OnEnable, Start and Update get executed per GameObject. This can cause quite a few issues when for example the Update function of Script A requires a value of script B, which only gets set in the Start function.\n\nSo far, the only workaround seems to be to modify the execution order.\n\nAlso, the order in which GameObjects get called is different between Editor and InGame, but that is probably a different issue.",
